WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.670
Duck Dynasty's Robertson clan has become Louisiana's
de facto first family.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:10.690
Despite patriarch Phil Robertson's well-known
controversial statements to GQ, some secrets

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:14.019
still remain tucked away behind those big
bushy beards.

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:18.670
Let's look past the bird calls and shotguns
and explore the untold truth of Duck Dynasty's

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.859
Robertson family.

00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:22.390
Censor charade

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.820
Phil Robertson's faith is no secret, but apparently
the folks at A&amp;E thought they could keep it

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.609
a secret early on in the show's production.

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:34.010
Robertson told Sports Spectrum in 2013 that
during the show, the editors would add some

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.989
bleeps to the audio to make it look like the
family members were swearing, but he insisted

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:39.819
no vulgarity was used.

00:00:39.819 --> 00:00:44.160
He also alleged that producers edited out
the words "in Jesus's name" during a family

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.160
prayer filmed for the end of one early episode.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.829
According to Robertson, they did it because
"they don't want to offend some of the Muslims

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:52.429
or something."

00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:54.159
Heavy drinker

00:00:54.159 --> 00:00:59.239
Before he became vocal about his religious
beliefs, Phil Robertson was quite the hellraiser,

00:00:59.239 --> 00:01:00.760
according to his wife Miss Kay.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.210
In her book The Women of Duck Commander, she
writes that Phil's drinking cost him his job

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.210
as a teacher.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.210
Although what he taught has never been revealed,
it's known that he educated youngsters for

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:14.149
several years, and he also holds a master's
degree in education.

00:01:14.149 --> 00:01:18.970
Drinking also eventually cost the bearded
patriarch his subsequent job — running a

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:19.970
bar.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.600
Public image

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.740
Robertson's alcoholic past has clearly affected
him and his family — and alcohol has continued

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.030
to have an impact on their financial bottom
line.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:34.520
In 2013, son Willie Robertson launched his
brand of Duck Commander Wines, sold online

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.740
and at the finest Walmarts for $10 a bottle.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:42.549
According to Fox News, the staunchly anti-drinking
Christian group Family Ministries went on

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:44.369
to cancel an appearance with Willie.

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:47.939
Lucky for the Robertsons, this was only a
drop in the duck-calling bucket.

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:51.259
"Boom boom boom boom boom boom boom."

00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:52.539
Substance abuse

00:01:52.539 --> 00:01:56.630
Much like his father, Jep Robertson has had
troubles with substance abuse.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:01.850
Jep told I Am Second in 2013 that he has a
sordid history — with popping pills being

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.240
the least of what he did.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.049
He started seeing the warning signs of his
reckless lifestyle after one night when he

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:11.799
woke up after driving under the influence,
unable to remember where he came from or where

00:02:11.799 --> 00:02:12.799
he was going.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.470
"To this day I don't know what I did that
night.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:20.130
And I hope I didn't run over somebody, I don't
know."

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:25.230
That wasn't enough to get him to quit — but
shortly thereafter, his family staged an intervention.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.150
Since then, he's stayed on the straight and
narrow.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.400
Doubting Jase

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.650
They've earned the admiration of millions
for their supposedly strong faith, but the

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:37.599
Robertsons have had a doubting Thomas in their
midst — at least when it comes to their

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:39.209
television endeavors.

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:43.760
Second-eldest son Jason "Jase" Robertson didn't
think for a second that Duck Dynasty would

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.370
last one season, let alone lead the flock
to the fame and fortune they've received.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:49.659
"What is that?

00:02:49.659 --> 00:02:50.659
What's in the sink?"

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:51.659
"It's a beaver."

00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:52.659
"That's what's stinking."

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:57.189
He told Fox News Radio, "I had this perception
of reality shows that you had to have all

00:02:57.189 --> 00:03:00.519
this friction and fits of rage and four-letter
words."

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:02.459
Luckily, Jase was wrong.

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:03.459
An honest mistake

00:03:03.459 --> 00:03:09.260
While visiting New York in 2013, Jase attempted
to stay at the Trump International Hotel,

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.830
but a hotel staffer booted him out due to
his ZZ Top-style beard.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:18.409
As Jase explained it, the staffer "was very
nice, he walked me outside, pointed down the

00:03:18.409 --> 00:03:20.720
road and said, 'Good luck,'" according to
People.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.549
Following the incident, the Trump family reached
out to apologize, and the Robertsons ended

00:03:25.549 --> 00:03:27.689
up hitting it off with Donald Trump Jr.

00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:30.239
Fame and misery

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:34.290
Jase's son, Reed Robertson, knows fame isn't
all it's cracked up to be.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:38.840
As he admitted during the family's interviews
with I Am Second, Reed's newfound fame initially

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.500
caused his ego to swell out of control.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:46.280
This resulted in him pushing his friends away
from him, both intentionally and unintentionally.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.090
Reed's isolation culminated in some potentially
suicidal thoughts.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:54.140
He credited his faith with getting him back
on track — and a stern talking-to from his

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.140
dad.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.530
"He told me, he said, 'That's the most selfish
thing you can do.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:02.560
To leave this world because you can't take
it.'"

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.480
Imperfect proposal

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:10.590
Fan favorite Silas Merritt "Uncle Si" Robertson
has only ever had eyes for one woman, his

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.500
wife since 1971 — Christine Raney.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:18.160
But his long-term admiration of her isn't
necessarily a good thing.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:23.570
Before they got married, Uncle Si asked for
her hand in marriage over 70 times before

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.440
she answered his bridal calls and said yes.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.260
Some people just don't take no for an answer.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.640
"Gimme a thousand dollars, we'll call it even."

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:31.750
"What is this, extortion?"

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.420
Now, you got a bad attitude!"

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.420
Thanks for watching!

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.700
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.850
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

